Description: keep a subrequest's own body length when the parent discards
 nginx 148c75678 (in 1.31.9) sends Content-Length 0 upstream while the
 request body is being discarded. In nginx a request that is discarding its
 body never has r->request_body, but subrequests inherit r->discard_body
 from their parent, and OpenResty modules attach a body of their own to a
 subrequest (ngx.location.capture{body=...}, echo_subrequest -b,
 srcache_store). Without this guard such a proxied subrequest announces
 "Content-Length: 0" and then sends the body bytes, desyncing a keepalive
 HTTP/1.1 upstream. Restrict the zero length to the case 148c75678 targets.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-18
---
--- a/bundle/nginx-1.31.8/src/http/modules/ngx_http_proxy_module.c
+++ b/bundle/nginx-1.31.8/src/http/modules/ngx_http_proxy_module.c
@@ -1307,7 +1307,7 @@
         ctx->internal_body_length = -1;
         ctx->internal_chunked = 1;
 
-    } else if (r->discard_body) {
+    } else if (r->discard_body && r->request_body == NULL) {
         ctx->internal_body_length = 0;
 
     } else {
--- a/bundle/nginx-1.31.8/src/http/modules/ngx_http_proxy_v2_module.c
+++ b/bundle/nginx-1.31.8/src/http/modules/ngx_http_proxy_v2_module.c
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@
     } else if (r->headers_in.chunked && r->reading_body) {
         ctx->ctx.internal_body_length = -1;
 
-    } else if (r->discard_body) {
+    } else if (r->discard_body && r->request_body == NULL) {
         ctx->ctx.internal_body_length = 0;
 
     } else {
